  "output": {"svg": "architecture.svg", "medium": "documentation and notebook", "alt_text": "A versioned but untrusted design packet passes strict schema validation and becomes an authority and effect graph. Human or model reviewers may propose threats, while deterministic versioned invariants consume producer-authenticated, tenant-bound, current evidence. Violations become actionable findings and a packet-bound PASS, BLOCK, or UNKNOWN review receipt. Named control and risk owners make a versioned repair, independent tests admit new evidence, and a separate authorized release gate decides whether to deploy."},
